{"chunk_id": "ab9be7162fc8", "text": "This passage depicts an extraordinary duel between the teacher Drona and his greatest pupil, Arjuna. Their combat mirrors perfect symmetry: every celestial weapon Drona invokes\u2014Aindra, Pasupata, Vayavya, and others\u2014is countered by Arjuna. Observers compare them to hawks battling in the sky, and even Drona silently praises Arjuna\u2019s mastery, seeing his own training reflected in the student. Heavenly beings gather to witness the spectacle, declaring it beyond ordinary human or divine warfare\u2014like Rudra fighting himself. When Drona unleashes the terrifying Brahma weapon, nature itself trembles, but Arjuna neutralizes it with one of his own. The stalemate dissolves into broader battle. In the next clash, Dhrishtadyumna drives back Duhsasana and advances toward Drona while Nakula and Sahadeva shield him. Amid intense combat, the warriors deliberately avoid unfair weapons, emphasizing a code of righteous warfare even within carnage.\nDrona and Arjuna fight an awe\u2011inspiring duel of celestial weapons, after which Dhrishtadyumna advances toward Drona amid fair battles among surrounding warriors.\nThemes: guru vs disciple duel, celestial weapons, warrior honor and fair combat, cosmic spectators, escalation toward Drona", "vector": [-0.007139486260712147, -0.005544351879507303, -0.020135635510087013, 0.01675059087574482, -0.002594192512333393, 0.023520678281784058, -0.02012220211327076, -0.003462281310930848, -0.02761765569448471, -0.03119075670838356, 0.006414119619876146, 0.007629780098795891, 0.010255875065922737, -0.002088786568492651, 0.010040951892733574, 0.006817101035267115, 0.04376377537846565, -0.00517495209351182, 0.007549183908849955, -0.027563923969864845, -0.025011708959937096, -0.007609630934894085, 0.002820869442075491, 0.021196819841861725, -0.01701924577355385, 0.023990822955965996, 0.013902856968343258, -0.03411908820271492, -0.001077975146472454, -0.011518550105392933, -0.007159635424613953, -0.0